{"body":{"text":["A paragraph holds its text, as runs: the text as written, its marks within it, *emphasis*, **strong**, `code` and links to the web, and a holon wherever something points at a part of it alone, lifted out and held in its place: a sentence a thread was raised in or a measure reaches, a link into the field, a term made on purpose. Nothing is lifted before something points there: \"a holon could be a paragrpah until something wants to point at only a sentance\" (19/45). A diff compares text, and a selection is a place in it: \"the component that does the diff simplu just has to compares trings, for selection we still allow char selections\"; \"rather we break down where needed for references\" (19/41). So holding grows finer only where something reaches in, as the author's grain would have it (18/55). *Settled, 19/45, \"I think it makes sense\" (19/47); built.*"]},"id":"1M82PT5J0NWE000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Words were holons once, and never at the author's asking: the second session read his words on locality, \"using sentences relationship and words relationship\" (2/6), as holons down to the word, its own path, and a later session kept them for fidelity (8/32), though he had settled only that a term is a holon of its own, made on purpose (8/33). \"why at each word, i have never asked for that, it doesnt make sense\" (19/37). A sentence something points at must be one: \"when a thread points to a sentance it needs to be a sentance, thats they way it is\" (19/43). The stores were folded once, through the engine: some 230,000 words and the holons of marks let go, and every sentence a thread or a measure points at lifted, 95 in all, so the field went from about 252,000 holons to 7,068, and Knowledge reads as text exactly as it did."]},"id":"1M82PT5J0NWE001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Nor is a lexicon stored beside the text: the words prose says are derived, by `lexicon()`, from the words each store's index cuts its text into, and the lexicon once stored, a second source of truth already apart from the first, is gone: \"of course we won't have a stored lexicon\" (18/103). *Settled, 18/103.*"]},"id":"1M82PT5J0NWE002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":"find(?b, [?b, \"instance\", @glass:prose/brief]) | size     how many briefs\nfind(?p, said(?p, \"text\", \"holon\"))                     every paragraph that says holon\noutline(@Knowledge, 2)                                  the shape of a brief, measured"},"id":"1M82PT5J0NWE003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000011"]}
{"body":{"text":["The site's build writes each store as it stands, its history's head and its index's and every blob they reach, gzipped, to `strata/<name>/`; the browser unpacks each with `DecompressionStream` before checking it against its name. The index is fetched, never built, since building would cost every visitor. What a read waits on is fetched at once, and, when a store is loaded whole, the rest after it, the index first. The store once called main came to 12.4 MB over the wire where it had been 119.8; its index arrives in 0.2 s and every blob in 4.6 s, reads answered all the while. The page keeps every store it opens whole: once a store has answered its first reads and been asked nothing for a moment, the rest is fetched behind any read, so the first view never waits on it, about 1 s, and moving within the field soon waits on nothing fetched, the whole field kept within some 7 s (19/31, 19/32)."]},"id":"1M82PT5J0NWE004","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Its commits are judged, minted and landed in strata, tested with stores that fail, refuse or answer changed every time, with many changes, and with two engines over one storage at once. The page at `/`, the command line and the author's tools all read and commit through it, and 258 tests pass. Before the earlier engine went, the new one was held to it question by question over every store: 60 the same, 11 refused by design, and 6 apart from the migration itself. It runs on Bun 1.4.4, since Bun 1.3.11 lost a message now and then on MessagePorts between workers."]},"id":"1M82PT5J0NWE005","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Reading Knowledge as text takes about 0.36 s at the command line over the five stores, where it took 0.8 s while every word was a holon (19/47). On the site a brief opens in 60 to 210 ms once the field is fetched, after the brief's read was found entering every brief beneath it, its stop lost behind a placeholder the engine matches by type (19/39). The engine still lets go of what a use gives beyond what its function takes, without a word, which is to be refused, since nothing is to fail silently (19/39). Still between: `language/text.ts` keeps the earlier form of expressions for its own tests alone."]},"id":"1M82PT5J0NWE006","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then, committed through the engine, every expression was written again as uses, once for good; glass's types were grouped, a second function type and the paper's own prose types let go for glass's, and the markdown forms and the types nothing used let go. Git keeps only each store's history, about 48 MB, and each index is rebuilt from it. Since prose was folded to its text, the five hold about 7,000 holons where they held 252,000 (19/47). *Proposed, 18/104; built.*"]},"id":"1M82PT5J0NWE007","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The site is published as the repository's pages on GitHub, built from main by its workflow at every push, on the author's own domain (19/25). The build copies each store and prepares its index, copying a store only once its heads hold still and failing rather than publish one missing a blob its heads name (19/30); GitHub's cache may keep a head some 10 minutes after a deploy, naming blobs the deploy no longer has; that the published site might instead read the repository itself, as git serves it in plain files, is the git integration's to show (19/21, 19/24)."]},"id":"1M82PT5J0NWE008","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}